@.str.81 = private unnamed_addr constant [2144 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Run the default app from the `blender-bin` flake:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix run blender-bin\0A  ```\0A\0A* Run a non-default app from the `blender-bin` flake:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix run blender-bin#blender_2_83\0A  ```\0A\0A  Tip: you can find apps provided by this flake by running `nix flake\0A  show blender-bin`.\0A\0A* Run `vim` from the `nixpkgs` flake:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix run nixpkgs#vim\0A  ```\0A\0A  Note that `vim` (as of the time of writing of this page) is not an\0A  app but a package. Thus, Nix runs the eponymous file from the `vim`\0A  package.\0A\0A* Run `vim` with arguments:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix run nixpkgs#vim -- --help\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0A`nix run` builds and runs [*installable*](./nix.md#installables), which must evaluate to an\0A*app* or a regular Nix derivation.\0A\0AIf *installable* evaluates to an *app* (see below), it executes the\0Aprogram specified by the app definition.\0A\0AIf *installable* evaluates to a derivation, it will try to execute the\0Aprogram `<out>/bin/<name>`, where *out* is the primary output store\0Apath of the derivation, and *name* is the first of the following that\0Aexists:\0A\0A* The `meta.mainProgram` attribute of the derivation.\0A* The `pname` attribute of the derivation.\0A* The name part of the value of the `name` attribute of the derivation.\0A\0AFor instance, if `name` is set to `hello-1.10`, `nix run` will run\0A`$out/bin/hello`.\0A\0A# Flake output attributes\0A\0AIf no flake output attribute is given, `nix run` tries the following\0Aflake output attributes:\0A\0A* `apps.<system>.default`\0A\0A* `packages.<system>.default`\0A\0AIf an attribute *name* is given, `nix run` tries the following flake\0Aoutput attributes:\0A\0A* `apps.<system>.<name>`\0A\0A* `packages.<system>.<name>`\0A\0A* `legacyPackages.<system>.<name>`\0A\0A# Apps\0A\0AAn app is specified by a flake output attribute named\0A`apps.<system>.<name>`. It looks like this:\0A\0A```nix\0Aapps.x86_64-linux.blender_2_79 = {\0A  type = \22app\22;\0A  program = \22${self.packages.x86_64-linux.blender_2_79}/bin/blender\22;\0A};\0A```\0A\0AThe only supported attributes are:\0A\0A* `type` (required): Must be set to `app`.\0A\0A* `program` (required): The full path of the executable to run. It\0A  must reside in the Nix store.\0A\0A\00", align 1
